IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 58: PROCEEDINGS ARISING OUT OF HIRE-PURCHASE AGREEMENTS (3 rules).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A MAYBE BOOLEAN answer is:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (the FALSE-kind comment quotes them).
--   NOTHING     the text does not answer on these facts (the NOTHING-kind comment says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: every requirement in the Rules is subject to the Court's
-- discretion to order otherwise in the interests of justice; it is not threaded as an input.
-- What follows non-compliance with a Rule is O 3 r 2(4) (the Court "may" waive it, reject the document,
-- dismiss, and so on); the functions below that say NOTHING for a "must" not done cite that provision.
-- Judgment calls QA to QE are tagged "QX:" in comments; work/forks.py lists them for the fork register.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 58 -- proceedings arising out of hire-purchase agreements`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6887 | 1. These Rules apply to proceedings under the Hire‑Purchase Act subject to the following Rules.
@ref O 58 r 1 (src:6887)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under the Hire-Purchase Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 58 r 1 these Rules apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are under the Hire-Purchase Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "These Rules apply to proceedings under the Hire" names the proceedings it reaches and says nothing of others

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- mode of application under the Hire-Purchase Act`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The sections of the Hire-Purchase Act that rule 2 names.  The Act is not among the sources.
DECLARE `o 58 r 2 section of the Hire-Purchase Act` IS ONE OF
    `o 58 r 2 section 5(3)`
    `o 58 r 2 section 10`
    `o 58 r 2 section 32`
    `o 58 r 2 section 43`
    `o 58 r 2 section 44`
    `o 58 r 2 another section`

-- src:6889 | 2. An application under section 5(3), 10, 32, 43 or 44 of the Hire‑Purchase Act must be made by originating application supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application.
@ref O 58 r 2 (src:6889)
GIVEN section IS A `o 58 r 2 section of the Hire-Purchase Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 58 r 2 the section is one that the Rule names` MEANS
    section EQUALS `o 58 r 2 section 5(3)`
    OR section EQUALS `o 58 r 2 section 10`
    OR section EQUALS `o 58 r 2 section 32`
    OR section EQUALS `o 58 r 2 section 43`
    OR section EQUALS `o 58 r 2 section 44`

-- "must be made by originating application supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application".
-- The document used is a core `Document kind`.
-- src:6889 | 2. An application under section 5(3), 10, 32, 43 or 44 of the Hire‑Purchase Act must be made by originating application supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application.
@ref O 58 r 2 (src:6889)
GIVEN section IS A `o 58 r 2 section of the Hire-Purchase Act`
      document IS A `Document kind`
      `the application is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 58 r 2 the application is made as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`o 58 r 2 the section is one that the Rule names` section)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under section 5(3), 10, 32, 43 or 44 of the Hire" names the sections it reaches
        IF document EQUALS `Originating application` AND `the application is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must be made by originating application supported by an affidavit"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance) / other: JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- particulars to be included in the statement of claim`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What the claimant's statement of claim gives.  Items (e) and (f) are required only "if any": an
-- amount claimed as due and unpaid, and any other claim; the two flags say whether there is one.
DECLARE `o 58 r 3 particulars given` HAS
    `o 58 r 3(a) gives the date of the agreement and the parties to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 58 r 3(b) gives the goods let under the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 58 r 3(c) gives the amount of the hire-purchase price` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 58 r 3(d) gives the amount paid by or on behalf of the hirer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 58 r 3(e) an amount is claimed as due and unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 58 r 3(e) gives that amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 58 r 3(f) there is another claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `o 58 r 3(f) gives the amount of that claim and the circumstances in which it arises` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:6891 | 3. Where the claimant’s claim is for the recovery of money arising out of a hire‑purchase agreement, the claimant must, in the claimant’s statement of claim, give the following particulars: ( a )
@ref O 58 r 3 (src:6891)
GIVEN `the claimant's claim is for the recovery of money arising out of a hire-purchase agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 58 r 3 the duty to give the particulars arises` MEANS
    IF `the claimant's claim is for the recovery of money arising out of a hire-purchase agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is for the recovery of money arising out of a hire-purchase agreement" (the Rule's "Where" condition is unmet; ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:6891 | 3. Where the claimant’s claim is for the recovery of money arising out of a hire‑purchase agreement, the claimant must, in the claimant’s statement of claim, give the following particulars: ( a )
-- src:6892 | the date of the agreement and the parties to the agreement;
-- src:6893 | ( b )
-- src:6894 | the goods let under the agreement;
-- src:6895 | ( c )
-- src:6896 | the amount of the hire‑purchase price;
-- src:6897 | ( d )
-- src:6898 | the amount paid by or on behalf of the hirer;
-- src:6899 | ( e )
-- src:6900 | the amount (if any) claimed as being due and unpaid in respect of any instalment or instalments of the hire‑purchase price;
-- src:6901 | ( f )
-- src:6902 | the amount of any other claim and the circumstances in which it arises.
@ref O 58 r 3 (src:6891-6902)
GIVEN given IS A `o 58 r 3 particulars given`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`o 58 r 3 the particulars still to be given` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (IF given's `o 58 r 3(a) gives the date of the agreement and the parties to the agreement` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the date of the agreement and the parties to the agreement"),
        (IF given's `o 58 r 3(b) gives the goods let under the agreement` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the goods let under the agreement"),
        (IF given's `o 58 r 3(c) gives the amount of the hire-purchase price` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the amount of the hire-purchase price"),
        (IF given's `o 58 r 3(d) gives the amount paid by or on behalf of the hirer` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the amount paid by or on behalf of the hirer"),
        (IF (NOT (given's `o 58 r 3(e) an amount is claimed as due and unpaid`)) OR given's `o 58 r 3(e) gives that amount` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the amount (if any) claimed as being due and unpaid in respect of any instalment or instalments of the hire-purchase price"),
        (IF (NOT (given's `o 58 r 3(f) there is another claim`)) OR given's `o 58 r 3(f) gives the amount of that claim and the circumstances in which it arises` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "the amount of any other claim and the circumstances in which it arises"))

-- src:6891 | 3. Where the claimant’s claim is for the recovery of money arising out of a hire‑purchase agreement, the claimant must, in the claimant’s statement of claim, give the following particulars: ( a )
-- src:6892 | the date of the agreement and the parties to the agreement;
-- src:6893 | ( b )
-- src:6894 | the goods let under the agreement;
-- src:6895 | ( c )
-- src:6896 | the amount of the hire‑purchase price;
-- src:6897 | ( d )
-- src:6898 | the amount paid by or on behalf of the hirer;
-- src:6899 | ( e )
-- src:6900 | the amount (if any) claimed as being due and unpaid in respect of any instalment or instalments of the hire‑purchase price;
-- src:6901 | ( f )
-- src:6902 | the amount of any other claim and the circumstances in which it arises.
@ref O 58 r 3 (src:6891-6902)
GIVEN `the claimant's claim is for the recovery of money arising out of a hire-purchase agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      given IS A `o 58 r 3 particulars given`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 58 r 3 the statement of claim gives the particulars` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the claimant's claim is for the recovery of money arising out of a hire-purchase agreement`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the claimant" conditions the duty; QD: NOTHING, and the companion `o 58 r 3 the duty to give the particulars arises` answers JUST FALSE / other: JUST TRUE (nothing is unmet)
        IF count (`o 58 r 3 the particulars still to be given` given) EQUALS 0
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bare "must ... give the following particulars"; QB: NOTHING (O 3 r 2(4) says what the Court may do about non-compliance) / other: JUST FALSE
